  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Counter Trafficking in Persons Efforts in Montenegro</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As a response to the latest US Trafficking in Persons Report (TIP Report) released in June 2023, which downgraded Montenegro to the Tier 2 Watch List, this project will take a holistic approach and tackle both policy and operational levels of work as to enhance the counter trafficking response in Montenegro at local level. The overall objective of the 24-month project is to empower the Counter TIP office and the Operational Team for Combating Trafficking in Human Beings, enabling them to enhance coordination among local and national stakeholders responsible for the identification and response to suspected TIP cases. At policy level the project will seek to improve the work and coordination among relevant stakeholders by defining protocols on cooperation and identifying roles and responsibilities. Moreover, an analysis of the local response capacities, including the available victim support referral, will produce recommendations for the improvement of entire local response structures. The project will work on strengthening capacities of different interlocutors at operational level, through a series of capacity building activities focused on identification of potential victims of trafficking (VoTs) and referral systems.</narrative>
  </description>
